      "text": [
        ": «خَمْسَةٌ لاَ يَؤُمُّونَ اَلنَّاسَ وَ لاَ يُصَلُّونَ بِهِمْ صَلاَةً فَرِيضَةً فِي جَمَاعَةٍ اَلْأَبْرَصُ وَ اَلْمَجْذُومُ وَ وَلَدُ اَلزِّنَا وَ اَلْأَعْرَابِيُّ حَتَّى يُهَاجِرَ وَ اَلْمَحْدُودُ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.bab-ul-qaim-publications": [
          "Hadith.1104 - Muhammad ibn Muslim narrated from Imam Muhammad ibn Ali Al-Baqir (as) who said:\n\"Five people should not lead others in prayer nor should they lead them in a congregational obligatory prayer: the person with leprosy (abrāṣ), the person with a skin disease (majdhūm), the child of adultery (walad al-zina), the Bedouin (a‘rābī) until he migrates, and the person who has been subjected to the legal punishment (al-maḥdūd).\""
        ]
      }
    },
